hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:
"590","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up at night to offer Tahajjud prayer, he would say: ""O Allah! All praise is for You; You are the Disposer of the affairs of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, and all praise is for You; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, and all praise is for You; You are the King of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, and all praise is for You; You are True, and Your promise is true, and meeting You is true, and Your word is true, and Paradise and Hell are true, and all the Prophets are true, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah! I am obedient to You, and I have believed in You, and I have put my trust in You, and I turn to You, and with Your help I argue with the opponents, and I appoint You as a judge. So forgive my past and future sins, my hidden and open sins; You are the One Who brings forward and Who delays; there is no deity except You."" Or he said: ""There is no true deity except You."""
"591","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whoever saw a dream would narrate it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I also wished that I would see a dream and narrate it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was a young man and during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I used to sleep in the mosque. So (one day) I saw in a dream as if two angels had caught me and were taking me towards Hell. Suddenly (I saw that) it was like a well, winding, and it had two pillars. There were some people in it whom I recognized. So I began to say, “I seek refuge in Allah from Hell.” Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that then we met another angel and he said to me, “Do not be afraid.” I narrated this dream to Umm al-Mu’minin Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) (who was the sister of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both), and Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Abdullah is a very good man, if only he would pray Tahajjud!” After that, Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to sleep very little at night."
"592","Narrated Sayyiduna Jundub bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became ill, so for one or two nights he did not get up (for Tahajjud prayer)."
"593","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one night to him and Sayyidah Fatimah az-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her), the daughter of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: ""Why do you both not pray (at night)?"" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Our souls are in Allah's control, so when He wishes to wake us up, He will wake us up."" When I said this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back and did not reply to me. I heard that as he was leaving, he was striking his thigh with his hand and saying: ""And man is more quarrelsome than anything."""
"594","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would abandon a deed, even though he loved it, out of fear that people would act upon it and it might be made obligatory upon them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never performed the Duha prayer, but I perform it."
"595","Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stand (in prayer) so long that both his feet or (he said) both his shins would swell. So it was said to him (that do not exert yourself so much in worship), and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would reply: “Should I not be a grateful servant of Allah?”"
"596","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""The prayer most beloved to Allah is the prayer of Dawud (David), and the fasting most beloved to Allah is the fasting of Dawud. He would sleep half the night, pray for one third of it, and then sleep for one sixth of it. And he would fast one day and not fast the next day."""
"597","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The deed which could be done consistently was beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The narrator says: I asked, ""At what time would the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) get up (at night)?"" She said: He would get up when he heard the crowing of the rooster."
"598","In one narration, (Ash'ath says) that when the Prophet (peace be upon him) heard the crowing of a rooster, he would get up to perform the Tahajjud prayer."
"599","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says in another narration that I found the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) sleeping beside me in the last part of the night."
"600","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): I prayed the night prayer (Tahajjud) with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he kept standing (in prayer) until I intended to do something bad. He was asked: What did you intend? He replied: I intended to sit down and leave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing."
"601","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` the prayer of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be thirteen rak'ahs, that is, at night."
"602","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night; among them were the Witr and the two (Sunnah) rak'ahs of Fajr."
"603","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would sometimes refrain from fasting in a month to such an extent that we would think he would not fast at all in that month. But when he began to fast in a month, he would fast continuously until we thought he would not leave any day without fasting in that month. And regarding his (praying and sleeping), his condition was such that if you wished to see him praying at night, you could see him, and if you wished to see him sleeping, you could see him."
"604","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you goes to sleep, Satan ties three knots at the back of his neck. On each knot he breathes the following words: 'The night is long, so keep sleeping.' If he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. If he performs ablution, the second knot is undone. And if he offers prayer, the third knot is undone, and he rises in the morning energetic and with a cheerful heart. Otherwise, he gets up in the morning sluggish and with a lazy disposition."""
"605","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): A man was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was said that he sleeps till morning and does not get up for (Tahajjud) prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Satan urinates in his ears."""
"606","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Our Lord, the Most Great and Most Exalted, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains, and He says: 'Is there anyone who will supplicate to Me so that I may answer his supplication? Is there anyone who will ask of Me so that I may grant him? Is there anyone who will seek forgiveness from Me so that I may forgive him?'"""
"607","It was asked from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): ""How was the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night?"" She said: ""He (peace be upon him) would sleep at the beginning of the night and would get up in the last part of the night and pray. After the prayer, he would return to his bed, then when the muezzin gave the call to prayer, he (peace be upon him) would get up; if he needed to, he would take a bath, otherwise he would perform ablution and go out."""
"608","It was asked from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in Ramadan, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not pray more than eleven rak'ahs in Ramadan or outside of Ramadan. (First) he would pray four rak'ahs, so do not ask about their excellence and their length, then after that he would pray another four rak'ahs, so do not ask about their excellence and their length, then after that he would pray three rak'ahs of Witr. Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I said, O Messenger of Allah! Do you sleep before praying Witr? So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."""
"609","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): (Once in the mosque) the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and (saw that) a rope was hanging between two pillars. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""What is this rope?"" The people replied that this rope was hung by Umm al-Mu'mineen Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her); when she becomes tired while standing in prayer, she holds on to this rope. The Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No, this should not be done at all. Untie it. Each of you should pray as long as he feels energetic, and when he becomes tired, he should sit down."""
"610","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once said to me: ""O Abdullah! Do not be like so-and-so; he used to get up at night for prayer, then he abandoned getting up at night and praying."""
"611","Narrated by Sayyiduna ‘Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever gets up at night and says: ‘There is no deity except Allah, He is One, He has no partner, His is the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He is powerful over everything. All praise is for Allah, and Allah is pure, and Allah is the Greatest, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah’s help.’ Then says: ‘O Allah! Forgive my sins,’ or makes any supplication, his supplication will be accepted. Then if he performs ablution and offers prayer, his prayer will be accepted.”"
"612","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he began mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in his sermon, and he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once said: ""Your brother (Abdullah bin Rawahah, may Allah be pleased with him) does not utter vain things (see how he expresses truthful themes in these verses): 'Among us is Allah’s Messenger who recites to us His Book when the dawn breaks. We were blind, and he showed us the way. His word is certain, which settles in the heart. At night, he keeps his side apart from his bed, while sleep weighs heavily on the beds of the disbelievers.'"""
"613","´Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) says that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I saw this (dream) that it was as if there was a piece of istabraq (silk cloth) in my hand, and it was as if wherever in Paradise I wanted to go, it would carry me there flying, and I saw that two persons came to me. The rest of the hadith has passed earlier. (See the Book: Description of the Night Prayer... Chapter: The Virtue of the Night Prayer, i.e., Tahajjud...)"
"614","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us to perform Istikhara (seeking guidance from Allah) in all matters (and with such emphasis) as he used to teach us a Surah from the Qur'an. He (peace be upon him) used to say: ""When any one of you intends to do any work, he should offer two rak'ahs of prayer other than the obligatory prayer and (after the prayer) say: 'O Allah! I seek goodness from Your knowledge and I seek power from Your might and I ask You from Your great bounty. Surely, You have power and I have no power, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah! If You know that this matter is good for me in my religion, my worldly life, and the outcome of my affairs, then ordain it for me and make it easy for me, and if You know that this matter is harmful for me in my religion, my worldly life, and the outcome of my affairs, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and ordain for me what is good wherever it may be, and make me pleased with it.'"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""And he should mention his need (to Allah)."""
"615","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not observe any voluntary prayer as regularly as he observed the two rak'ahs (Sunnah) before Fajr."
"616","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer very lightly, to the extent that I would say (in my heart) whether he (peace be upon him) had even recited Umm al-Qur'an (i.e., Surah Al-Fatiha) or not."
"617","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says` My close friend, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), advised me regarding three things which I will not leave until I die. These three things are: (1) Fasting three days every month, (2) Performing the Duha (forenoon) prayer, (3) Sleeping after offering Witr prayer."
"618","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) never used to leave four rak'ahs before Dhuhr and two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"619","`Sayyiduna Abdullah Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: ""Perform voluntary prayers before the Maghrib prayer."" (He said this three times) and the third time he said: ""Whoever wishes."" He (peace be upon him) did not like that people should consider this as Sunnah (therefore, he gave the choice that whoever wishes may perform it and whoever wishes may leave it)."
